# Aggregator topology (hub side).
#
#   Remote_Source(s) ─→ Remote_Job_Rewrite ─→ Topic (firehose:topic)
#
# Remote_Job_Rewrite flips aggregated k:"job" entries to k:"remote_job" so they
# dispatch on the hub via newspack_nodes/remote_job_handlers; non-job entries
# pass through. The firehose Topic is the multi-partition, KEY-routed sink.
#
# `firehose` is a Vault_Group over Vault group `spoke`: it builds one
# Remote_Source per member, `{id}` substituted for each Vault id, and follows
# the Vault on reload — a spoke is added or dropped by editing group
# membership, never by hand-editing this file. Never hand-wire a second
# Remote_Source for a spoke already in the group beside it: two readers
# pulling the same spoke partition under independent cursors double-ingest
# every entry.
#
# assume_clean_shutdown and set_multi_writer are recorded ONCE, on the group,
# and replayed to every child present now or built later. connect_node's
# target is likewise the group's own, replayed the same way: it is also the
# relay's DECLARATION of where a spoke's lines may go, since a firehose record
# carries no TO of its own and the relay refuses any line a spoke addressed
# rather than letting it name a node in this worker's graph — the refusal
# consumes the line, and the cursor advances past it.
#
# set_multi_writer belongs on every firehose spoke: the log is appended by every
# request process there, and it asks the SPOKE's reader to hold a superseded
# segment for the seal grace. Without it a straggler's last line — typically the
# request's terminal `process (complete)` — is orphaned, and the request never
# finalizes on the hub.
#
# The offsetlog + deadletter templates are the group's own ARGUMENTS (each
# child reads like the Consumer it is). Scope the cursor with `<topology>`: an
# offsetlog is a reader's cursor and the reader is the FLEET, so two hubs
# pulling one spoke partition must not share one. Omit them and you get no
# cursor / no quarantine — Consumer's contract.
#
# Each substrate Remote_Source is self-sufficient (it patrons its own SSE_In +
# HTTP_Out, owns its offsetlog, and publishes a status snapshot under the
# install-scoped cache key remote:<node-name>:<remote_partition>, e.g.
# remote:firehose:<id>:firehose.p0). SSL/HTTPS policy comes from the substrate
# vault_verify_ssl / vault_require_ssl config — not a per-topology setter.
#
# A Vault id colliding with an already-declared node name (e.g. `topic`) is
# skipped loudly rather than aborting the load, because this group is declared
# AFTER the nodes it could collide with — keep it last among the make_node
# lines below.

include topic-probe

make_node Remote_Job_Rewrite remote-job-rewrite
make_node Topic firehose:topic <config:logs_dir>/firehose.p{partition}
make_node Vault_Group firehose Remote_Source spoke firehose.p<partition> <config:offsets_dir>/<topology>.firehose.{id}.p<partition> <config:deadletter_dir>/<topology>.firehose.{id}.p<partition>

command_node firehose:config assume_clean_shutdown true
command_node firehose:config set_multi_writer true
connect_node firehose remote-job-rewrite
connect_node remote-job-rewrite firehose:topic

secure
